DATA SOURCES (each bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useExportJobs        → ExportsRepository.exportJobs() (GET /export/jobs)  → exportsState
  useBulkExportsDelete → ExportsRepository.bulkExportsDelete(ids) (POST /export/jobs/bulk) → deleteSelected()
  exportDownloadUrl    → shared-core exportDownloadUrl(jobId) (/api/v1/export/jobs/{id}/download),
                         opened under BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL via LocalUriHandler (ExportsPage.kt L484)

  S8 NOTE: the Android DI graph (DataContainer) wires no ExportsStore, and the shared S8 ExportsStore
  exposes no public on-demand refresh for the error-retry affordance (it re-fetches only via mutation
  invalidation). So — exactly as the sibling A7 DrivesListPage binds the shared DrivingRepository — the
  host constructs the shared S7 HttpExportsRepository over the SAME resilient client + offline cache, and
  the ViewModel is the lifecycle-aware StateFlow projection that owns the refresh trigger. No predecessor
  is bypassed: the S7 repository IS the KMP core data port the S8 store itself delegates to.

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  No field on this surface is unit-bearing (file sizes are raw bytes, timestamps are ISO strings), so
  there is no SI conversion. The only render-boundary transformation is display formatting:
  formatExportBytes (bytes → B/KB/MB/GB) and formatExportDateTime (ISO → localized date-time), matching
  the web formatBytes / formatDateTime. ADR-013 keeps the cached payload raw.

