STRING CATALOG
  16 of the 19 keys already existed in res/values/strings.xml (generated from the shared i18n catalog).
  The 3 missing keys were added to res/values/strings.xml with the verbatim web inline-default values
  (ExportsPage.tsx) — `res/values*/strings.xml` is an allowed file:
    translation_exportsList_subtitle              "Manage your past export jobs. Select rows to delete in bulk."
    translation_exportsList_empty_body            "Your future exports will appear here for download or deletion."
    translation_exportsList_bulk_deleteConfirm_body "Selected jobs and their downloadable artifacts will be permanently removed."
  The selectExport interpolation uses positional %1$s (translation_exportsList_selectExport), and the
  bulk count chip reuses the existing plurals translation_bulk_selected + translation_bulk_ofTotal with
  the parity noun (exportsList.noun.one/other), so no StringFormatInvalid is raised. The dynamic
  `exportsList.status.${status}` web key has no catalog entry on either platform, so the raw status
  string is rendered verbatim — the exact web `t(key, j.status)` fallback (ExportStatusBadge L471).

